<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle market at standstill - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle market at standstill - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading on slaughter steers and heifers was at a standstill, USDA said.</p>
<p>Large weekly movement cleaned up showlists and put packer live inventories in good shape. Few $110.00 per cwt bids on a dressed basis were available Thursday morning.</p>
<p>Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered ( paid on hot carcass weights).</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -  No reported sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter heifers - No reported sales.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed - None   For the week - 99,500</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
